        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Escaped flowerhorn cichlids are causing concern for native species and about parasites capable of infecting humans</p><p>Escaped ornamental aquarium fish have integrated into a local ecosystem in the Philippines, but scientists say they may be threatening the native biodiversity of the lake.</p><p>Flowerhorn cichlids – human-bred hybrid fish prized for their bright-gold colour and prominent head humps – are believed to have escaped from breeding facilities into Lake Sampaloc, which sits in a volcanic crater, during a typhoon.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/17/biodiversity-fears-flowerhorn-cichlids-philippines-lake\">Continue reading...</a>"
